# mod_GLQS_readme
*clr
cla
'<b>Version 0.38.0 - Current</b>'
'- Added: Two more ways to open GLQS. Settings > Mods now has an Open GLQS link on the GLQS row, and every tab of the built-in cheat menu has one at the bottom. Return takes you back to where you came from, and that screen still exits to wherever you were before. The switch that hides the room link is now on the GLQS Index.'
'- Fixed: Clothing store screens had lost the store icon, name and instructions.'
'- Fixed: The Owned / Not owned links on Consumables never changed anything. Every click wrote to an empty inventory slot instead of the item.'
'- Changed: Consumables now lists every item Set All touches, with readable names. 39 items were being filled without being shown. Set All also gives one of each single item, such as the pregnancy ball or skipping rope.'
'- Changed: Enable All and Disable All in Recurrent Cheats run the addiction, vibrator and dirty-clothes rows through the same handlers the game uses when you click them. Clear Addiction Levels now also clears cocaine and painkiller withdrawal.'
'- Fixed: Max Succubus Skills now raises the stored energy cap straight away, so Feed fills to the new cap.'
'- Fixed: Clear Penalties on a job now also resets the missed-shift warning count, so the next missed shift is reported again.'
'- Changed: Relationships now says what Max does. It sets every listed character to 100, including ones you have not met.'
'- Changed: Tattoo zones and piercing slots are listed as links with the current design number next to each.'
'- Changed: Maxing fame recalculates each activity once instead of once per region, so Max All Fame does 17 recalculations instead of 68.'
'- Changed: Jobs Max Rank goes through the game rank setter, and the readme Return button goes straight to the Mods tab instead of through a retired redirect.'
'- Changed: Internal cleanup. Every data table now uses one row format read by one shared splitter, temporary tables are no longer left in save files, and the build reports a bad character as a lint error with its line number instead of crashing.'
'<b>Version 0.37.0</b>'
'- Fixed: Every clothing grant wrote to the same array slot, so picking an item from the store picker added the first item in that category instead of the one you clicked, and Give All added a single item. Affected v0.36.1 only.'
'- Fixed: Give Everything (all stores) and Buy All (this store) added nothing at all. The clothing catalog gained a label column in v0.36 and the buyout loop was still reading three columns, so every category key it built had the label stuck on the end and matched nothing in the game. Roughly 1,900 grants per click were going nowhere.'
'- Fixed: Max All Skills & Attributes set maximum Willpower to a flat 150. That is the cheat menu cap, but character creation allows up to 200, so a character built above 150 had it reduced by a button labelled Max All. It now only ever raises.'
'- Fixed: Enable All in Recurrent Cheats switched on Succubus clothing invulnerability even when clothing archetypes were disabled, where that row is hidden, leaving the cheat set with no way to see or clear it. Disable All can still clear one that was already on.'
'- Fixed: Filtering Relationships to Male Only or Female Only could leave a category heading and its Max link with no names underneath, because the heading was written before the filter was applied. Gadukino and Outcasts under Female Only were the clearest cases.'
'- Changed: Health & Energy reads maximum mana from the value the game already maintains instead of recalculating it from a copied formula.'
'- Changed: The build now refuses two mistakes that used to compile silently - a numeric value read from the string argument slot, which is what caused the clothing grant bug above, and a generated action block that was never filled in.'
'<b>Version 0.36.1</b>'
'- Fixed: Normalized the source fragment numbering after the menu/clothing/consumables reorganization so there are no missing numbered files and the build manifest matches the actual file layout.'
'- Fixed: Cleared stale filename references in the build validation and docs so the assembled mod, clothing catalog, and job data continue to resolve correctly after the renumbering cleanup.'
'<b>Version 0.36.0</b>'
'- Changed: Top-level menu tabs reordered by function instead of their old ad-hoc order - Appearance (Clothing, Body Mods), Character (Skills & Attributes, Health & Energy, Grades & Academics, Magic), Social (Relationships, Fame & Reputation), Economy (Money, Jobs & Career, Housing & Property, Consumables, Lifestyle), with Recurrent Cheats last since its a toggle-heavy meta menu rather than a character system.'
'- Added: Relationships roster grew by 33 NPCs across two new categories - Gadukino (village residents) and University (friends and professors) - plus six additional family members, all pulled from the base games own NPC data rather than guessed.'
'- Added: Relationships now has a Status link per NPC opening a picker for Dating/Boyfriend/Girlfriend/Fuckbuddy/Sugar Daddy, using the games own lover gosub handlers so old-status cleanup and stat counters stay correct exactly like a real relationship change would.'
'- Added: Relationships has a Trigger Random Lover Encounter (Male/Female) button, jumping straight into the games own blind-date event instead of waiting on the RNG-gated street encounter.'
'- Added: Relationships now scans the games own npc_index array for procedurally-generated NPCs (background characters promoted through random encounters) that have an active relationship status, listing them under Generated NPCs with the same Max/Status actions as the named roster.'
'- Added: Lifestyle now covers phone plans - Grant Unlimited Phone Plans activates both Mobile Internet and Calls & Texts permanently, bypassing the bank-account requirement and monthly charge entirely.'
'<b>Version 0.35.1</b>'
'- Fixed: Recurrent Cheats Clear Addiction Levels only zeroed secondary withdrawal-timer counters (heroin_hours_addicted/taper, caffeine_need/dose, amphetamine_withdrawl) and never the underlying heroin_used, heroin_need, caffeine_system, and amphetamine_used counters that heroin_stat/caffeine_stat/amphetamine_stat re-derive addiction from on every gs stat pass - so those three substances silently re-addicted on the very next menu load even though painkiller and cocaine, whose root counters were already cleared, worked correctly.'
'<b>Version 0.35.0</b>'
'- Added: Quick-nav bar under every top-level menus title, including the Index - one click between any two of the 15 top-level screens instead of Return to Top Menu then drill back in, with the current screen shown in place of its own link so it cannot be clicked again. Not on nested sub-screens (store detail, tattoo/piercing pickers, fame by region) - those already have their own Return/Back.'
'- Added: Menu display style toggle, available from every top-level menu - Action Buttons (default, the original look everywhere) or Text Links (renders the nav bar as inline hyperlinks instead, closer to the base games own Cheat Menu tab bar). Switching reloads whichever screen you are currently on. Every other menus own action buttons (Give Everything, Max All, etc.) are unaffected either way.'
'- Added: Jobs & Career submenu - Instant-Hire at any of the games 28 defined jobs (bypasses the interview/hiring quest entirely, matching how set_employed itself only guards against double-hiring), Max Rank / Boost Pay / Clear Penalties per currently-held job, and Ignore Job Schedule Conflicts (reuses the games own existing cheatVars[work] debug hook).'
'- Added: Lifestyle submenu, bundling three small systems the same way Recurrent Cheats bundles small toggles - Max Casino Chips, Clear All Pain (reuses the base games own pain-clearing cheat exactly), and Max All Fetish Experience/Preferences across all 23 fetishes via the games own validated setter API.'
'- Added: Grades & Academics (renamed from School Grades) now covers university - Force Enroll (Nursing/Teaching Studies) and Grant University Diploma. Deliberately does not try to instant-pass individual semesters - each ones grades are formula-chained off the prior semester and the games own semester-tracking variable has an inconsistently-used typo twin, not confidently safe to drive by hand.'
'- Added: Recurrent Cheats has a Clear Addiction Levels button - the existing immunity toggle only stops new addiction from building, it never touched already-built-up tolerance/dependency (painkillers, caffeine, cocaine, heroin, cigarettes, amphetamines), so a save with prior drug use kept suffering withdrawal even with the toggle on.'
'- Added: Housing & Property now covers the players car - Grant a Car (via the real add_car gosub, since car IDs are not a free integer and a raw write leaves it half-initialized), Repair & Un-wreck, and Full Tank.'
'- Added: Magic now shows Succubus Stats and, if active, Instant Max Level / Feed / Max Skills / Remove & Reset (reuses the base games own reset cheat) - mirrors the base games own character sheet, which renders succubus stats inside the same Magic tab. Also adds Become a Succubus, skipping straight to the fully-active state since the quest-stage values in between are either unimplemented content or the permanent-decline dead end.'
'- Added: Health & Energy now covers pregnancy - Force Pregnancy and Remove Pregnancy, both reusing the base games own cheat handlers exactly (Force Pregnancy spawns a throwaway donor NPC internally, so no NPC picker is needed).'
'- Added: Money now covers arrest/legal trouble - Clear Arrest Record zeroes the fine, deadline, and miss-counters on both arrest-tracking systems in the game and clears the pending court-date/hearing events that would otherwise re-trigger the cycle the next day. Writes the fields directly rather than paying off the fine through the money system, since a cheat that costs real cash defeats the point.'
'- Added: Magic submenu - shows mana and known-spell counts, Learn All Spells (every Combat/Non-Combat/Story spell the base games own Magic tab lists) and Max Mana. Shows the games own unable-to-use-magic message for no-magic characters instead of forcing magic on, since other systems may branch on that start-type choice in ways not auditable from here.'
'- Added: Relationships now shows each NPCs status (dating, boyfriend, husband, etc.) and, gender-matched, a Marry or Divorce link. Marrying/divorcing routes through the games own add_husband/add_wife/remove_husband/remove_wife so the one-husband-one-wife tracking ($husID/$wifID) never desyncs from $npc_rel_type - Marry only appears while that slot is empty.'
'- Added: Housing & Property submenu - shows homeless/current home/renovation/construction/rent status, Max Rent Days on every currently-rented property, and Finish Construction on the current home. Deliberately does not grant access to a new home or fix homelessness - property codes are not universal across game starts, so guessing one risks pointing the current home at a property that does not exist for that save.'
'- Fixed: Skills & Attributes display labeled Inhibition as (0=uninhibited), backwards from the mods own long-standing convention (100=uninhibited, 0=fully inhibited, per the v0.6 changelog and confirmed against the base games own audition dialogue) and from what Max All Skills & Attributes already sets it to.'
'- Fixed: Buying a purse via Give Everything / Buy By Store / the item picker never called purse_attributes first, unlike every other clothing category. The base games own add_item does, and skips granting when PursePrice is 0 (not a real purse for that brand/index) - GLQS now matches that guard.'
'- Changed: Removed Return to Top Menu from the piercing jewelry screen (Body Mods, Choose a Piercing, pick a slot), matching the v0.28.1 tattoo design screen decision - Back to Slots already covers it at that depth.'
'- Changed: Skills & Attributes now lists every skill Max All Skills & Attributes actually sets (was 17 of ~40, e.g. Basketball, Wrestling, Hacking, and every Artistic skill were maxed but never shown), grouped to match the games own Mental/Combat/Sport/Beauty/Artistic/Work categories.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.34.9</b>'
'- Changed: Mod renamed from GLQS Rolling to GLQS (Girl Life Quick Start). Purely a branding change to the mods own description text - the mod id, save data, and everything else stay the same.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.34.8</b>'
'- Changed: Quick Setup link now only shows in the players own room - home bedroom, uni dorm room, or the therapist hotel room - instead of on almost every real location in the game. Restores the mods original pre-0.29.12 scope.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.34.7</b>'
'- Fixed: Full Restore Everything in Health & Energy set Hunger to 200, but the base games real cap is 100. The excess silently converted to body fat on the very next in-game hour, the opposite of a max stats cheat. Now sets it to the correct cap of 100.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.34.6</b>'
'- Added: Health & Energy display and Full Restore Everything now include Faith, a new stat the base game added for the prude archetype.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.34.5</b>'
'- Fixed: Money submenu showed raw cash and bank balances instead of using the base games own overflow-safe formatter, so totals silently underreported once a balance passed the roughly 1 billion RUB point where the games own balance packing kicks in. Now uses the same formatter the games persistent money display uses.'
'- Fixed: Relationships was missing Zina, a real Nerds-category relationship character the base game tracks - she could never be viewed or maxed from this menu.'
'- Fixed: Max All Skills and Attributes, and the Skills and Attributes display, omitted Songwriting - a real, active skill the base game tracks alongside Singing and Instruments. Now included in both.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.34.4</b>'
'- Fixed: Max All Skills & Attributes wrote the five volleyball sub-skills (block, receive, serve, set, spike) directly, but the game recomputes all five from the main Volleyball skill and the attributes on every stat refresh, so those writes were discarded immediately and never did anything. Removed - maxing Volleyball and the attributes already maxes all five.'
'- Fixed: Granting an item the character already owned (Give Everything, Buy All, Give All, or a single item pick) kept its old dirt and tailor-alteration state instead of arriving factory-fresh. The base games own add_item purchase code resets those arrays on every purchase; the grant code now does the same.'
'- Fixed: Body Mods listed the tattoo counter as out of 17 zones, but the game (and the mods own zone picker) has 18 tattoo zones.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.34.3</b>'
'- Fixed: The Misc clothing category (Give Everything, Buy By Store, and the per-item picker) granted a wall of blank, unlabeled clothing slots - as many as whatever category happened to run right before it internally. Root cause: this category was keyed to an array named misc, but the base game only ever defines images and descriptions for a differently-named misc_outfits array (which holds exactly one scripted item, not a real shop line) and has no official item count for misc at all, so the count silently carried over from the previous category in the buy-out list instead of stopping at zero. The broken Misc category has been removed entirely - there was never a real shop behind it to buy out.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.34.2</b>'
'- Fixed: Every clothing item granted through Quick Setup (Fill categories, Give All, Give This Item) reported This item is too small for you to wear as soon as you tried it on. The grant code set every clothing attribute except the body-size fit value the base game bakes in when you actually buy an outfit, so it was left at 0 and always failed the fit check against your real hip size. Now set the same way the base games own add_item/resize_clothes routines do.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.34.1</b>'
'- Changed: Quick Setup link no longer shows on the wardrobe screen or the shared clothing_view browsing/buying screen every store routes through - purely cosmetic, so it does not clutter these image-heavy screens. Nothing else depends on the link being present there.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.34</b>'
'- Added: School Grades has a Zero Absences button, separate from Set All Grades to 100, matching the base games own Zero Absenteeism cheat menu option.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.33</b>'
'- Fixed: Fame By Region (individual activity Max buttons and Max All (this region)) silently did nothing for every activity except Sex, Prostitution and Flashing - those three looked unaffected only because they already carry decent fame from normal gameplay, not because the buttons worked. Root cause: fame_detail killed the captured region variable at the end of its own render, before the player could click any button that used it, so every max click ran with an empty region and wrote to a bogus fame key instead of the real one. This is the same stray-killvar bug the v0.28 changelog already fixed once; the v0.29.4 shared-data-table refactor reintroduced it here.'
'- Fixed: Same stray-killvar bug also broke Remove Tattoo From This Zone and Remove Piercing From This Slot in Body Mods - both killed the captured zone/slot before the button using it could be clicked.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.32.1</b>'
'- Changed: Consumables - Individual toggles now read Owned/Not owned instead of Enabled/Disabled, since these are physical items rather than behavior flags.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.32</b>'
'- Fixed: 14 of the items added to Consumables in v0.30 (breastmilk bottles, thrush medication, hair extension shampoo, a butt growth injection, joints/cocaine/amphetamine, foraged berries/mushrooms, and household supplies) are stackable in the base game, not capped at 1 like the items that remain in Individual toggles - moved them into Set All to 10,000/1,000/100 instead of a fixed on/off value.'
'- Added: Consumables - Exercise Equipment toggle category (skipping rope, hula hoop, book on yoga, ice skates, skis, refillable water bottle). These were already granted silently by Set All as part of a generic unique-items grant; pulling them into their own toggles gives each one visibility and individual control, matching the base games own Sport Equipment shop catalog.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.31</b>'
'- Added: Recurrent Cheats - every item in the main list now toggles individually by clicking it, not just via Enable All/Disable All. Also added two cheats the base games own cheat menu has that GLQS was missing entirely: Porn schedule editor and No dream chance (skip bad dreams).'
'- Fixed: Never get addicted, Enable sleeping with vibrator inserted, and Clothes never dirty now call the same handlers the base games own cheat menu uses instead of only flipping the flag, so enabling them also clears existing addiction progress, syncs the bed vibrator setting the sleep menu actually checks, and washes everything currently dirty, matching base game behavior.'
'- Changed: Succubus clothing invulnerability only shows while Clothing archetypes is enabled, matching the base games own cheat menu - it has no effect otherwise.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.30</b>'
'- Added: Consumables now has an Individual toggles section below Set All, covering 20 items the base games own cheat menu and item catalog expose that Set All did not: breastmilk bottles (S/M), thrush medication, hair extension shampoo, a butt growth injection, narcotics (joints, cocaine, amphetamine), bottled water/sandwich/wine, foraged berries and mushrooms, household supplies (dishwashing detergent, clothing detergent, plates), and pregnancy support (morning sickness pills, pregnancy ball/brace/pillow). Kept separate from Set All and toggled individually so items like narcotics are not forced on a playthrough that is not using them - the same reasoning Recurrent Cheats already uses for its own individual toggles.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.29.13</b>'
'- Fixed: Skills & Attributes listed the def skill as Defence; corrected to Defense to match the base games own skill label.'
'- Changed: Internal cleanup - removed stray excess blank lines that had accumulated in a few src fragments. No player-visible change.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.29.12</b>'
'- Changed: The Quick Setup link now shows up on every real location in the game (previously only the bedroom, dorm room and therapist hotel room), since it turns out the mod was already being invoked everywhere by the games own mod loader - it was just being filtered down to those 3 screens. Hidden during character creation and the games own scripted scenes (sex scenes, big story beats) so it does not show before your character fully exists or interrupt a scene. Still does not appear during ordinary NPC chat screens, which do not carry a signal this mod can detect.'
'- Fixed: The Return link now returns to the exact screen you opened Quick Setup from, using the same location tracking the game itself uses, instead of a value that was only reliably set if you had recently visited a shop.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.29.11</b>'
'- Fixed: The Quick Setup link (bedroom/dorm/hotel) was hidden by default on every new save until you found and enabled the Quick Setup Mod toggle buried in the games own cheat menu. Now enabled automatically the first time - the toggle is still there in the cheat menu if you ever want to hide the link.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.29.10</b>'
'- Removed: The experimental Purse screen Quick Setup link from v0.29.9. Confirmed by live testing it never appeared - the purse is a plain subroutine overlay rather than a real location change, so it does not update the game state the bedroom/dorm/hotel links rely on to detect where the player currently is.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.29.8</b>'
'- Added: Max Attractiveness button in Body Mods. Forces the underlying appearance base high enough that attractiveness always reads as maxed regardless of clothing, accessories, or grooming state. Only applies until the next in-game day, same as School Grades - click again to reapply.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.29.7</b>'
'- Fixed: Recurrent Cheats - Impregnation toggle was always shown even while Periods and pregnancies was disabled, where it silently did nothing (conception in the base game only runs as part of the normal menstrual cycle, which Periods and pregnancies fully halts). Now hidden in that state, matching the base games own cheat menu.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.29.6</b>'
'- Changed: Recurrent Cheats - Impregnation, Lactation, Cum leaking, STDs, Periods and pregnancies, and Clothing archetypes each got their own individual toggle instead of being bundled into Enable All/Disable All, since those six affect more significant game state (fertility, disease risk, clothing-archetype trait progress) than the other quality-of-life toggles. Enable All/Disable All no longer touch these six at all - previously both buttons silently forced all six to the same off state no matter which was clicked, so there was no way to turn any of them on from this menu.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.29.5</b>'
'- Changed: Internal refactor, no player-visible change. Fame By Region (activity list + labels) was hardcoded in two places (fame_detail and fame_maxregion); they now share one data table, so the copies can no longer drift out of sync. build.py also now checks that mod_info and the changelog version agree, so this specific number cannot silently drift again.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.29.4</b>'
'- Note: Fame By Region - Max All (this region) only sets that regions own fame directly, but the games own fame-spread system then bleeds some of that into the other regions too (working as designed - e.g. maxing Pavlovsk also pushes Old Town and Gadukino close to maxed, since fame spreads fast between those, while City only gets a small bump since it is slow to notice fame from Pavlovsk). This is base game behavior, not a mod bug.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.29.3</b>'
'- Fixed: Relationships menu threw a Bracket not found error on open. The v0.29.2 refactor built the NPC value cell as a template marker split across a string concatenation, which QSP does not allow. Now reads npc_rel directly as a value instead of through a template marker.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.29.2</b>'
'- Changed: Internal refactor, no player-visible change. Relationships (roster + category maxing) and the clothing store catalog (store_buy and the Give Everything handler) each used to hardcode the same NPC list or store/category list in two or three places; they now share one data table each, looped over at render/apply time, so the copies can no longer drift out of sync.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.29.1</b>'
'- Added: Store icon shown at the top of the store category list and the item picker screen.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.29</b>'
'- Changed: Clothing categories (e.g. Allure - Swimsuits) now open an image grid like the tattoo/piercing pickers instead of instantly buying every item in the category. Click an item to add just that one, or use Give All (this category) to still buy the whole category in one click.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.28.2</b>'
'- Changed: Updated the mod description (shown in the games mod list) to cover everything GLQS actually does now - money, relationships, health, body mods and fame were missing from it.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.28.1</b>'
'- Changed: Removed Return to Top Menu from the tattoo design screen (Body Mods, Choose a Tattoo, pick a zone) - Back to Zones already covers it at that depth.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.28</b>'
'- Fixed: Fame By Region (individual activity buttons, Max All This Region, and the live table) still did not apply. Root cause: the region code was captured from ARGS after calling stat/themes, which clobber the shared ARGS array just like any nested gs call, and a stray killvar was clearing the captured region before the player could click a button. Same fix applied to the clothing per-store screen and the tattoo/piercing pickers, which had the same latent bug.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.27</b>'
'- Fixed: Fame maxing (individual activity, Max All This Region, Max All Fame) silently did nothing and the live table always read 0. Root cause: same ARGS clobbering bug as the v0.7 grades fix - re-reading ARGS after a nested gs call back into mod_GLQS_main picked up the callees ARGS instead. Fixed by capturing region/activity into local variables before any nested call.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.26</b>'
'- Added: Fame & Reputation now shows live values - a per-region overview table (Performer, Sex Industry, Slut/Sex Rep, Sport) on the region picker, and a full per-activity fame table on each region screen, matching the Skills & Attributes style.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.25</b>'
'- Added: Fame & Reputation submenu now has a By Region breakdown (Pavlovsk, City, Old Town, Gadukino) with an individual Max button per activity, plus a Max All (this region) option, alongside the existing Max All Fame (everything) button.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.24</b>'
'- Added: Fame & Reputation submenu with a Max All Fame button covering every activity (acting, dance, painting, music, ballet, modelling, porn, stripping, kickboxing, running, volleyball, chess, teaching, media, sex, prostitution, flashing) across all four regions.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.23</b>'
'- Added: Every submenu now has a Return to Top Menu button that jumps straight back to the main Quick Setup screen, in addition to any existing one-level-back navigation.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.22</b>'
'- Added: Buy By Store submenu now breaks each store down into individual category buttons (e.g. Panties, Bras, Outfits, Shoes) instead of one buy-everything action, plus a Buy All (this store) option.'
'- Fixed: Store category submenu used single-line if statements with a trailing end, which QSP does not allow - it desynced block parsing for the rest of mod_GLQS_main and caused an Unknown action error. Removed the invalid end from every single-line if.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.21</b>'
'- Added: Per-category [Max] link next to each relationship category header (Family, Popular Kids, Athletes, Nerds, Gopniks, Outcasts, Teachers, Others), respecting the gender filter.'
'- Changed: Tattoo/piercing image galleries now use a wrapping grid layout instead of stacking vertically.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.20</b>'
'- Changed: Body Mods now lets you pick a zone/slot and browse actual tattoo and piercing designs by image, instead of a single Give All button. Electrolysis unchanged.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.19</b>'
'- Fixed: Apostrophes inside !! comments (e.g. games, cheat_repair) broke the parser - the game engine does not fully suppress quote-parsing inside comments, so a lone apostrophe opened an unterminated string that corrupted all block-nesting after it. Removed all apostrophes from comments.'
'- Changed: Individual store buttons in Clothing & Accessories moved behind a Buy By Store submenu.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.18</b>'
'- Added: Per-store buy-out buttons in Clothing & Accessories.'
'- Fixed: Clothing no longer needs tailor repair/resize. Root cause was the companion _h[] durability array never being set, defaulting to 0.'
'- Added: Body Mods submenu (free electrolysis, tattoo every zone, piercing every slot).'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.17</b>'
'- Added: Money submenu (open bank account, give cash/bank funds).'
'- Added: Relationships submenu showing and maxing key NPC relationships.'
'- Added: Health & Energy submenu with full restore.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.16.1</b>'
'- Added: Consumables submenu now has Set All to 10,000 / 1,000 / 100 options.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.15</b>'
'- Removed: Do Everything option.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.14</b>'
'- Fixed: Max All Skills & Attributes was redirecting to the cheat menu. setSkills and setAttrs both end with gt cheatmenu_din which hijacks navigation. Replaced with direct setStat calls for every skill and attribute.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.13</b>'
'- Added: Clothing, Consumables and Skills & Attributes all now open their own submenus showing live data before applying changes.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.12</b>'
'- Changed: Grades moved to its own submenu showing live grade values.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.11</b>'
'- Fixed: Grades re-added. Root cause: grade_cap=0 clamped all grade_award calls to 0 in nested gs context. Fixed with 13 flat direct calls.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.9</b>'
'- Fixed: Consumables completely rewritten using correct mc_inventory[''name''] system.'
'- All old variable names (prezikcount, tampon, etc.) were legacy/wrong - replaced with 67 correct mc_inventory keys.'
'- Added full coverage: beauty, medical, contraceptives, drugs, food, sex toys, magazines, unique equipment.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.8</b>'
'- Dropped: Grades support removed. The grade system requires school initialization (createclass/grade_cap) that cannot be reliably set from a mod context.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.7</b>'
'- Fixed: Grade variables now set class cap to 100 before assigning grade directly.'
'- Fixed: ARGS[1] was being clobbered by inner gs calls inside fill_grade loop.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.6</b>'
'- Fixed: Syntax error caused by inline !! comments after code (QSP only supports !! at start of a line).'
'- Fixed: Em dash characters in comments caused parser crash.'
'- Fixed: Attributes now use gs ''shortgs'', ''setStat'' directly (setAttrs needed $att_name[] pre-populated at startup).'
'- Fixed: Grade storage uses class[''school_X_grade''] not gschoolVars. Grades are 0-100 not 1-5.'
'- Fixed: Inhibition raw value is inverted - 100 = uninhibited, 0 = fully inhibited.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.5</b>'
'- Fixed: Inline !! comments partially addressed. Attribute variable names corrected from game source.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.4</b>'
'- Fixed: Skill and attribute variable names corrected using cheatmenu_din source code.'
'- Added: Skills, attributes and grades option (grades still broken at this point).'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.3</b>'
'- Added: Max Skills / Attributes / Grades option (all variable names wrong, fixed in later versions).'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.2</b>'
'- Fixed: Clothing now unlocks from ALL stores, not just visited ones.'
'- Root cause: arrsize() returns 0 for unvisited store arrays. Fixed by using each category totals subroutine.'
*nl
'<b>Version 0.1 - Initial Release</b>'
'- All clothing and accessories from every store.'
'- 10,000 of all consumables (variable names were wrong, fixed in 0.9).'
*nl
act 'Return': gt '$menu_settings', 'mods'
